WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:18.066
The rain continued for a week, but Mary didn't mind.

2
00:00:19.447 --> 00:00:22.328
She spent hours every day with Colin in his room.

3
00:00:23.629 --> 00:00:26.530
They talked about rajahs and gardens and Dickon.

4
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.892
They looked through Colin's books and took turns reading to each other.

5
00:00:32.244 --> 00:00:35.025
Colin was still pale and lying on his sofa.

6
00:00:36.665 --> 00:00:40.646
But Mary thought he looked much better when he was amused or interested in something.

7
00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:48.728
Mrs. Medlock noticed something too: Colin hadn't whined or had a tantrum since he and Mary had become

8
00:00:48.888 --> 00:00:55.750
friends. Mary still didn't want to tell Colin that she had actually seen the secret garden.

9
00:00:56.991 --> 00:01:01.692
But he seemed so pleased with the idea of the garden that perhaps she could trust him after

10
00:01:01.832 --> 00:01:07.626
all. She did want him to go outside and meet Dickon, unless of course he didn't want to

11
00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:08.247
meet Dickon.

12
00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:11.689
Colin was never happy when people looked at him.

13
00:01:11.709 --> 00:01:17.612
"I always hated that, even when I was little," he told Mary one day.

14
00:01:17.632 --> 00:01:22.715
"When I was taken to the seaside, ladies would stop and talk to my nurse.

15
00:01:24.035 --> 00:01:26.897
I knew they were talking about how I wouldn't live to grow up.

16
00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:30.499
Sometimes the ladies would pat my cheek.

17
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.994
Once I screamed out loud and bit a lady right on the hand.

18
00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:38.075
She was so frightened, she ran away!"

19
00:01:38.095 --> 00:01:42.038
"She probably thought you were a mad dog."

20
00:01:42.558 --> 00:01:44.819
Mary did not approve of what Colin had done.

21
00:01:44.839 --> 00:01:47.381
"I don't care what she thought."

22
00:01:48.721 --> 00:01:50.182
Mary hesitated for a moment.

23
00:01:50.202 --> 00:01:53.244
"Would you care if my friend looked at you?"

24
00:01:54.805 --> 00:01:56.286
Colin lay back on his cushion.

25
00:01:56.306 --> 00:01:59.688
"I believe there's one person I wouldn't mind.

26
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.902
It's that boy who knows where the foxes live—Dickon.

27
00:02:05.163 --> 00:02:09.827
The birds and other animals aren't bothered by him," Colin said, still thinking it over.

28
00:02:09.847 --> 00:02:12.248
"So perhaps I wouldn't mind either.

29
00:02:13.549 --> 00:02:17.132
He's a sort of animal charmer, and I'm a sort of boy animal."

30
00:02:18.373 --> 00:02:21.535
And at that he and Mary both burst into laughter.

31
00:02:23.416 --> 00:02:27.940
On the first morning when the sky was blue again, Mary woke up before anyone else.

32
00:02:30.076 --> 00:02:31.957
She ran to her window and opened it.

33
00:02:33.677 --> 00:02:38.278
The moor looked so blue, and the singing birds sounded like an orchestra warming up.

34
00:02:39.699 --> 00:02:42.479
A gust of fresh, scented air blew into the room.

35
00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.600
Mary stuck her hand out the window.

36
00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.621
"It's warm!

37
00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.802
That will make the flowers push up and up in the garden."

38
00:02:52.622 --> 00:02:56.123
She leaned out the window and drew in great breaths of fresh air.

39
00:02:57.464 --> 00:02:58.744
Suddenly she had an idea.

40
00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:00.861
"I can't wait!

41
00:03:01.241 --> 00:03:02.422
I'm going to see the garden!"

42
00:03:03.703 --> 00:03:05.524
By now Mary could dress herself.

43
00:03:06.925 --> 00:03:10.247
In five minutes she had put on her clothes and run outside.

44
00:03:11.548 --> 00:03:13.410
The beautiful day filled her with joy.

45
00:03:14.711 --> 00:03:17.793
When she reached the door to the secret garden, she stopped.

46
00:03:20.895 --> 00:03:22.256
Caw! Caw!

47
00:03:22.276 --> 00:03:22.897
Mary looked up.

48
00:03:24.278 --> 00:03:27.220
There, on top of the wall, was a big black crow.

49
00:03:28.648 --> 00:03:32.492
Mary had never seen a crow up close before, and she was a little nervous.

50
00:03:33.893 --> 00:03:38.297
Just as she was wishing it would go away, it flew into the secret garden.

51
00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:45.403
When Mary pushed open the door, she saw that the crow was perched in an apple tree.

52
00:03:46.804 --> 00:03:52.028
A fox was lying underneath the tree, and they were both watching Dickon digging in the ground.

53
00:03:52.048 --> 00:03:54.010
"Oh, Dickon!

54
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:54.751
You're here!"

55
00:03:55.231 --> 00:03:55.852
cried Mary.

56
00:03:57.696 --> 00:03:59.657
"I couldn't stay away when the garden was waiting."

57
00:04:01.298 --> 00:04:03.980
The crow flew down and landed on Dickon's shoulder.

58
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.821
"This is Soot," he said.

59
00:04:08.082 --> 00:04:10.323
The red fox wandered over to meet Mary.

60
00:04:10.343 --> 00:04:12.524
"And this is Captain.

61
00:04:13.805 --> 00:04:15.746
Now you must see what's new in the garden."

62
00:04:16.987 --> 00:04:20.008
The two children ran from one part of the garden to another.

63
00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:26.092
Dickon showed Mary the swelling leaf buds on the rose branches that had seemed dead.

64
00:04:27.392 --> 00:04:31.374
He showed her what seemed like thousands of new green points pushing through the dirt.

65
00:04:32.794 --> 00:04:35.235
And best of all, he showed her the robin.

66
00:04:36.536 --> 00:04:40.957
The bird was fluttering about, carrying bits of twigs and straw to build a nest.

67
00:04:42.198 --> 00:04:43.298
He had found a mate.

68
00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:49.201
While they worked in the dirt, Mary told Dickon about meeting Colin.

69
00:04:50.401 --> 00:04:52.382
"Do you really think he wants to die?"

70
00:04:53.703 --> 00:04:55.323
Dickon stopped digging for a moment.

71
00:04:56.724 --> 00:04:59.053
"No, but he wishes he'd never been born.

72
00:05:00.435 --> 00:05:02.917
Mother says that's the worst thing on earth for a child."

73
00:05:02.937 --> 00:05:07.201
"Colin is so afraid he'll grow into a hunchback.

74
00:05:08.482 --> 00:05:11.504
He says if he felt a lump coming, he'd scream himself to death."

75
00:05:11.525 --> 00:05:16.729
"If he were out here, he wouldn't be watching for lumps to grow on his back."

76
00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.892
"I know," said Mary.

77
00:05:19.912 --> 00:05:24.136
"I keep wondering if we could bring him here without anyone seeing us."

78
00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:29.287
Just then the robin landed nearby with a twig in its beak.

79
00:05:29.307 --> 00:05:33.211
"Keep building your nest," Dickon said to the bird.

80
00:05:34.512 --> 00:05:35.754
"You know we won't bother you.

81
00:05:37.135 --> 00:05:38.456
We're building a nest too.

82
00:05:39.637 --> 00:05:41.980
Just be sure you keep this garden a secret."
